---
code: lint-required-tools-missing
when-fires: --require-tools was given and a configured external linter is absent from PATH. cli/main.rs lint_command. {tools} lists them.
why: 27R section 4 dir-absent-is-info, inverted by explicit request: absence is advisory by default, and --require-tools is how CI says a partial lint must not read as a pass.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
true

-- replay --
$ dorc lint book.sh --require-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

(run):
  - info [checkbashisms:lint-tool-absent] Dorc did not find `checkbashisms` on PATH, so none of its checks ran. Install it, pass --no-tools to silence this note, or --require-tools to make a missing tool a hard error. (raw)
  - info [shellcheck:lint-tool-absent] Dorc did not find `shellcheck` on PATH, so none of its checks ran. Install it, pass --no-tools to silence this note, or --require-tools to make a missing tool a hard error. (raw)

dorc lint: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 2 infos across 1 file.
dorc: lint: error[lint-required-tools-missing]: `--require-tools` was given, but these lint
tools are missing from PATH: shellcheck, checkbashisms.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: lint-required-tools-missing
{{tool}} = "checkbashisms"
{{v0}} = "0"
{{v1}} = "s"
{{v2}} = "0"
{{v3}} = "s"
{{v4}} = "2"
{{v5}} = "s"
{{v6}} = "1"
{{v7}} = ""
{{tools}} = "shellcheck, checkbashisms"
